        "question": "What is the easiest way to find PII in my codebase?",
        "answer": "Run a static scanner in CI that matches common PII and secret patterns (SSN, card, email, phone, AWS/GitHub/Slack keys) across code and git history - tools like truffleHog, gitleaks, or a pii-detector. Pair it with a manual review checklist, because patterns miss context."
